@startuml
title GET /api/ai-agents-teams/runs/{run_id} — capability-scoped run inspection
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

actor "Run-URL holder" as Holder #FFD8C2
participant "AgentsTeamsApiSdk\n.getRun(runId)" as SDK #D5EAF7
participant "Embers API" as API #FFC9A8
participant "AgentsTeamsService" as Domain #CDEACC
participant "F1r3node\nread node" as Chain #FFE4A6

Holder -> SDK : getRun(runId)
SDK -> API : GET /api/ai-agents-teams/runs/{run_id}
API -> Domain : get_run(run_id)
Domain -> Chain : read the run ledger\n(retry until the finalized write with\nthe expected postcondition is visible —\nread nodes can briefly expose the\nprevious finalized revision)
alt run exists
  Chain --> Domain : ledger record + durable events
  Domain -> Domain : merge the two ordered audit\nsequences (durable events and\nledger events) on the rightmost\ncompatible anchor
  Domain --> API : RunState
  API --> SDK : 200 RunState
  SDK --> Holder : status, revision, events,\nwaits, grants, hashes
else unknown run id
  API <-- Domain : not found
  SDK <-- API : 404, no body
end

note over API #FFF0C7
Possession of the run URL is the read authority
(UUIDv7 capability); it grants no command
authority. The state is execution metadata only:
status, revision, public wait identifiers,
approval grants, event types, and content or
capability hashes — never prompts, outputs,
credentials, or artifacts.
end note
@enduml
